# lago-metabase — CVEs inside the upstream metabase.jar.
#
# Both entries are libraries Metabase bundles in its uberjar. We do not
# build Metabase from source, so the only lever is the pinned
# METABASE_VERSION; nothing we can install or patch fixes them today.
#
# v0.63.20 (this pin) bundles jackson-core and jackson-databind 2.21.7,
# which clears CVE-2026-91776, CVE-2026-91777, CVE-2026-89407 and
# CVE-2026-89425. Those lines are gone from this file.
#
# What is left, with the bundled version and what it would take:
#
#   lz4-java 1.10.4 -> needs 1.11.4. No Metabase release bundles it:
#     v0.63.20 ships 1.10.4, v0.64.1 ships 1.11.1. The finding is
#     insecure temp-file handling when the native library is extracted.
#     Exploiting it needs a second local user who can write to the
#     temp dir; the image runs one process as uid 65532.
#   mssql-jdbc 13.2.1 -> no fixed 13.x in the 0.63 line. Lago runs
#     Postgres; the SQL Server driver is bundled by Metabase and never
#     loaded, so this is not reachable in our deployment.
#
# Re-check trigger: clears itself when Metabase ships a release bundling
# lz4-java >= 1.11.4. Trivy silently skips entries that match nothing,
# so a stale line is harmless — prune on the next clean build.
